NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1067,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,4,3,2,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":4,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":3.0868,"rank":0.1503,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"WEV002502","role":"target","render":{"description":"A pool in which a mill sank; a pool in which hay wagons vanished and in which a coach disappears after a voice in the water asked where the man is, for the time has come. A will-o'-the-wisp above the pool means that someone will drown or that a house will be built.","place":null,"prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/45349"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV002004","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A light above a pool is seen as an omen of an accident. Later a boy drowns there who had got drunk out of grief at being rejected by a girl.","place":"Mussel","prov":"Gr.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43322","original":"Achter de boerderij van mijn broer in Mussel was in het \"oal daip\" - de Mussel A - een diepe kolk. Zw. Tuin ziet op een avond boven die kolk een licht branden. Ze vermoedt een komend ongeluk. En dit komt.\n'n Poos later is er een feest. Een jonge man - G.D. - vraagt een meisje, of ze 's avonds met hem uit wil. Ze heeft er geen zin in. \nVan verdriet drinkt hij zich dronken.\nLater heeft 't kind spijt van haar weigering, want D. wordt de andere dag dood uit de kolk gehaald.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[52.955,7.03889]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"WEV006902","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Prediction that something will happen by a canal; people with a light were seen crossing a road. Later a drowned boy was carried home along that path in the evening.","place":"Vriescheloo","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43572","original":"Veurloop.\nOabram zag nog meer. Wazzen es n poar jongelu, dei zoln troun-n. \nToun de haile boudel veurmekoar was, woln ze de meubels koopn in Winschootn. t Wicht gung dr op of en de jong zol den in Winschootn bie heur koom-m. Hai bedochde zuk en verdronk zuk in n wieke.  \nMoar, en hier gait mie t om, oal Oabram har al joarn van te veurn zegd:“Doar gunders bie de wieke gebeurt nog es n keer wat. Ik zai dr mensn deur t veld trekn; langs dei loane goan ze en koom-m bie dei boerderij oet. Misschain verdrinkt dr wel aine. Ik zai ook, dat ze n lichie bie zuk hebben.” \nEn net zo is t gebeurd. Bie oavend hebben ze de jong langs t zulfde pad van de wieke noar hoes brocht.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.06833,7.11389]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV007506","role":"helper","render":{"description":"A prediction that someone will drown in a canal within a day comes true.","place":"Veelerveen","prov":"Gr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44134","original":"Toun ze mit t knoal aan t groaven wazzen, moz dr in t leste nog n dam deurstookn wordn.\nWazzen verschaiden manlu bie aan t waark.\nToun kwam dr aine langs, bleef n rukje stoan en zee: \n\"Joa, 't is n mooi knoal worn; t is allaind zo jammer, dat dr binnen vaarntwintig uur ain in verdrinkn mout.\"\n\"Och, doe hest altied wat\", zeden de keerls, en zai smeetn hom mit n schop vol zaand noar de kop.\nMoar kiek, d ander dag, t luip teegn twaalf uur en de mensn woln gau eetn, zee dr n seldoat teegn zien mouder:\n\"Ik goa eerst nog eevn zwemmen heur, veur t eetn.\"\n\"Och, jong, blief hier toch\", zee ze, t is muide nait meer weerd.\"\nHai gung toch hen, mor is best verdronkn.\n\nAal dizze vertelsels binnen woar.\nIk heb ze zulf beleefd.","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[53.05583,7.12778]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Mussel.","Find Barlage on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[53.0125,7.05556],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Barlage"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3058,"rank":0.6075,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ046312","role":"member","render":{"description":"Never run in the middle of the road at night: a funeral procession may pass.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24424","original":"Wy woarden altyd warskôge: rin noait midden op 'e wei by joun of by nacht, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje passeare.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ102104","role":"member","render":{"description":"Some people had to get out of bed at night to see funeral processions. You should never run in the middle of the road at night.","place":"Augustinusga","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/37102","original":"Yn 'e Harkema en yn Stiensgea ha 'k wol guon kend dy't nachts fan bêd moesten om lykstaesjes to sjen.\nMen moest nachts noait midden op 'e wei rinne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"KOOIJMAN2266","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"You were warned not to walk in the cart track or on the bridle path at night. Because there you could meet evil spirits.","place":"Heesselt","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0333","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/127631","original":"Dat weet ik ook nog. Je werd gewaarschuwd om 's nachts niet in 't wagenspoor of in 't paardenpad te lopen. Want daar kon je de boze geesten tegenkomen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ052415","role":"member","render":{"description":"The narrator tells of two men who often saw funeral processions. You must never walk in the middle of the road, because an invisible funeral procession can drive you off the road.","place":"Surhuisterveen","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25234","original":"Douwe Stavasius fan Grinzer Pein seach lykstaesjes.\nBoardzer Bruining fan Boelensloane ek. Dy leeft noch.\nMen mat noait midden op 'e wei rinne, hwant der kin us in lykstaesje oankomme, sûnder dat men it sjocht. Dan wurde jo fan 'e wei ôfsmiten.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Heesselt belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1281,"rank":0.3431,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"Voda_022_16","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A clergyman saw his own funeral. Four men with a bier kept walking behind him all night. He later died on that same road.","place":"Eindhoven","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1977,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/129749","original":"Een geestelijke uit Oirschot zag eens zijn eigen begrafenis. Op een nacht ging hij van Oirschot naar Best. Daar hoorde hij achter zich iemand lopen. Toen ie omkeek, zag ie vier mannen die een baar droegen. Hij wilde wachten, maar toen hie stil bleef staan, bleven ook de dragers stilstaan. En als ie verder ging, gingen ook de dragers verder. Zo bleven deze vier mannen met de baar de gehele nacht achter de geestelijke lopen. Die was blij dat ie eindelijk in Best aankwam, waar hij van de schrik kon bekomen. Enige tijd later moest de geestelijke weer naar Best. Daar stierf hij plotseling. Toen droeg men het lijk van de geestelijke over dezelfde weg die hij gelopen had toen de dragers met de baar hem volgden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ099406","role":"omen","render":{"description":"When a dog howls eerily, someone in the neighbourhood will die within 4 days.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36651","original":"As in houn spûkgûlde seinen se, gong der binnen fjouwer dagen ien dea yn net to fiere omtrek.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ065203","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A group of boys once called names at an old woman who was said to be a witch. The woman made as if to jump across the four-metre ditch, and the boys ran off as fast as they could. She often had to get up at night to see funeral processions.","place":"Twijzelerheide","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27375","original":"Hjir wenne yn Twizelerheide in âld minske, dat wie Minne Ael, dy gong foar in tsjoenster troch. Hja wie nachts faek warber. Hja wenne oan 'e Swâdde. Dy wie sa'n fjouwer meter breed.\nOp in kear skelden in pear jonges har út, dy wienen oan 'e oare kant fan 'e Swâdde. Doe die se in pear stappen achterút en sei: \"Ik sil jim krije\", krekt as soe se in oanloop nimme.\nDoe naeiden dy jonges hurd út.\nHja moest der nachts út as der in lykstaesje ûnderweis wie.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","4 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":4},"on_success":{"chime":4,"digit":{"value":4,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P1","difficulty":0.9161,"rank":0.8022,"note":"All four name the same thing. That becomes the label. Don’t write ‘a beast’.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST276","role":"card","render":{"description":"The stiepelteken (mark in the doorpost) came about when a wit wief (white woman) threw the axe with which she was chasing a farmhand, and it landed in the doorpost of the barn door. The farmhand had challenged the witte wieven (white women) by bringing a spit to a spinning gathering and immediately running off again.","place":"Vasse","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"B.J.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13620","original":"Op veel plaatsen in Twente hoort men de volgende vertellingen.\nDe Witte Wiefkes hadden eens gasten of spinvisite. De knecht van een boer uit de buurt bracht er het spit heen; en toen als de wind weer terug naar huis te paard. Maar een der witte wiefkes zat hem met een bijl achterna. De knecht was echter eerder thuis. Zij wierp hem echter met de bijl na, die in den stipel (deurstijl achterdeur) bleef zitten en toen riep ze nog: \"Had ik mien eenen schoen zo gauw knupt als m'andren rupt, dan was doe 't gebraad west.\"","lang":"Standard Dutch; Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST280","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmhand walks past the Witte Wieven (white women) at night. Because he insults them, one of them chases him. The farmhand just manages to flee into a house. The axe the Witte Wief (white woman) threw lands in the stiepel (doorpost).","place":"Goor","prov":"Ov.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"J.W.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13624","original":"Witte Wieven waren hier bekend. Men geloofde dat ze ongeluk aanbrachten.\nEen verhaal gaat hier, dat een boerenzoon laat naat huis terugkeerde en langs een plek kwam, waar een wit wief een gebraad aan het spit ronddraaide. De boerenzoon beledigde haar, waarna het witte wief hem met een bijl achterna zette. Gelukkig voor de boerenzoon kon hij nog net de boerderij bereiken, voor het witte wief hem had ingehaald. Maar deze gooide hem nog de bijl achterna, die in de \"stiepel\" bleef zitten.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LYST075","role":"card","render":{"description":"At a wedding one of the guests remarks that they forgot to invite the witte wieven (white women). When someone mockingly calls out to the witte wieven, an axe is thrown at his head. He just manages to flee inside in time. The door still shows the marks of the axe. The witte wief (white woman) calls out that she could have caught him if she had not lost her little shoe.","place":"Zenderen","prov":"Ov.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"M.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13289","original":"Parallel met het verhaal van de \"spinvisite\" loopt ook 't verhaal van de \"brulfte\" (bruiloft) waar een van de gasten tegen de \"brulfteneugers\" opmerkt dat hij de \"nögste noabers\" n.l. de \"witte wieve\" heeft vergeten. De \"brulfteneuger\" laat dat niet op zich zitten, gaat naar buiten en nodigt \"de witte wieve\" uit, op spottende toon. Hij wordt onmiddelijk achterna gezeten, vlucht nog net binnenshuis, terwijl hem de bijl nagegooid wordt en 'n snee in de niendeure maakt die nog aan de kleinkinderen van het bruidspaar vertoond wordt. Hier hoort ook weer dezelfde klacht over 't schoentje bij, dat niet was vastgestrikt.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"ENGELB_13_014","role":"card","render":{"description":"A man who brings the spit to the hill of the Huns is then chased by a Hun with an axe. The man manages to get into the farmhouse; the Hun throws the axe after him, and it lands in the doorpost.","place":"Rossum","prov":"Ov.","year":1977,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/128541","original":"Spit brengen\nG.M.: Ja dee knecht van Scholtn möt dat doan hebn, den hef t spit doar op n Huunboarg bracht en den hef t peard bie zik had en tenminste zoa heb ik t wa es heurd verteln en doe hef he t spit hef he doar henbracht noa n Huunboarg en doe is het der tuskn oet goan, n Huun löaw’k noa met t haandbiel en doe is Schoolt zien knecht bie t Schoolt owwer n onderstn nienduur vlögn en doe hef n Huun hem nog noasmetn en t haandbielkn in in duurnpost smetn\nE.M.: Dat heb ik ok vaak heurd.\nG.M.: Zoa heb ik t vaak heurn verteln.\nE.M.: A’j dat oppervlakkig bekiekt, zo’j zegn. Dat kan hoast geelsnich, mer ja ik heb wa honderd moal heurn verteln.","lang":"Twente dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Read the four again. Look at what occurs in each of the four, not at what happens in them.","It is an object.","Begins with A. 3 letters."],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"0133515b4a0488e2","accepted_hashes":["7f4b36ff85c76e7c5cee0e91ffceedf4ea995c995b32fefc8b5834ce94458f3a","8132c2f47ff6008d6686e439ef8295a6c6c056faa049270528f2894b9a657f17","9b7b6404c5ccfbbc6ebd2fe707324e039aeb666dd7a542be6e978318cd70f9f9"]},"on_success":{"print_label":true,"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c4"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3147,"rank":0.9293,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KEUNING012603","role":"member","render":{"description":"Two white women are said to walk in the churchyard at night.","place":"Genum","prov":"Fr.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131651","original":"Der waerd ek sein, dat op it tsjerkhôf to Hegebeintum by nacht faek twa wite wiven omrounen.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ124006","role":"member","render":{"description":"At a haunted spot witte wieven (white women) dance at night.","place":"Mûnein","prov":"Fr.","year":1979,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/32288","original":"Oan 'e dyk to Readtsjerk spûken wite wiven, nei't se seinen. Dy dounsen dêr nachts om.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"YPFOE070d","role":"member","render":{"description":"The narrator is heading home with a few friends. On the way they meet a white girl moving quickly. She floats towards a cottage. They go to investigate. Later an old man hanged himself, and people say it was connected with this. The minister is very sceptical about the story.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":null,"initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12149","original":"Wite juffers\nWat ik hjir yn 'e Westerein sels sjoen ha. Dat is no lyn, ik tink sa'n fiif-, seis-, sânenfyftich jier. Myn kammeraat en ik gyngen de jûntiid om in oere of alve stadichoan nei hûs ta. Doe troffen wy in pear jongelju en dy hâlden ús oan. De man sei: 'Sjoch, wat is dêr? Dêr is in famke midden yn 'e sûkerei. By it hûs dêre is it allegearre út en tsjuster, mar hoe kin dan sa'n wyt famke der yn 't lân weze?' Doe seach ik it ek. Ik sei: 'Dan moatte wy dêr ris even sjen'. Mar dat famke avensrarde tige hurd en wy koenen sjen, dat it net gie, mar dat it sweefde. It hie de grutte sawat fan in gewoan famke, en sniewyt. Ik sei: 'No, sille wy ris sjen? …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LIJST033","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"The devil follows a woman on her way home in the evening.","place":"Baflo","prov":"Gr.","year":1954,"code":null,"initials":"T.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/14752","original":"I. De duivel\n1. Zijn U verhalen bekend over mensen, die de duivel gezien hebben of omgang met hem hebben gehad (met hem gedanst hebben, met hem kaart hebben gespeeld), of kent U andere verhalen, waarin de duivel een rol speelt?\nGelieve elk verhaal te noteren op een afzonderlijk blad papier en in elk verhaal duidelijk aan te duiden hoe de duivel voorgesteld wordt (met bokshorens, bokspoten, paardenhoeven, sik, staat enz.).\n\nDit hoorde ik als kind; 1899 was het. De dochter van de vrouw die het overkwam vertelde het. Haar moeder was (ook al op leeftijd wel eens laat van de boerderij gekomen waar ze werkte, bij slacht en dergelijke kon het wel eens wat laat in de avond worden. Bij zoo'n gelegenheid was zij eens door de duivel gevolgd. …","lang":"Standard Dutch; Groningen dialect","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Baflo belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.1331,"rank":0.9492,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ053309","role":"card","render":{"description":"One night a man suddenly sees two white women. The two women sit down on his cart. The man becomes so frightened that he quickly runs off.","place":"Ons Belang","prov":"Utr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25339","original":"Hjir ien út 'e Harkema ried us mei de boerewein op in nacht nei Readskuorre ta. Doe seach er dêr ynienen twa wite froulju foar him. Hy ried dêr mei de hynders lyk op yn.\nDoe kommen dy beide froulju yn 't wyt by him op 'e wein.\nHy woarde sa binaud, dat hy sette sokken en naeide út.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ044314","role":"card","render":{"description":"One night a man saw a woman in white walking along the tram rails. He warned her that the tram was coming. But she did not move. It was a white lady.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24127","original":"Ik kom us in kear let yn 'e nacht werom fan 't jounpraten. Ik roan op 'e Sintelwei nei Houtigehage. Doe wie dêr in frommes yn 't wyt. Sy wie op 'e raljes. Ik sei tsjin har: \"Frou, jo matte dêr wei gean, hwant de tram is op komst.\"\nMar sy sei neat werom en bleau hwer't se wie. 't Wie in wite juffer.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ000411","role":"sill","render":{"description":"Three naked women haunting the area chase a man, who has to run so hard that he sweats terribly.","place":"Nijega","prov":"Fr.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/11550","stain":"three"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ013206","role":"card","render":{"description":"Witte wijven (white women) haunt the Kruisweg in Harkema.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19522"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"YPFOE143","role":"card","render":{"description":"A woman has breast cancer. No herb can cure her. The only option is to go to Germany, to the white nuns. The nuns speak a magic formula and then make the sign of the cross. After this has been done several times, the patient may go home. Once she is home, she gradually gets better. In the end a tumour as big as a cauliflower falls out of her breast. The wound heals and she recovers completely.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":"TM 4302","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12993","original":"De wite susters fan Bremen\nIen fan 'e foarâlden fan myn frou—it is al lang Iyn—krige kanker yn 't boarst. Dêr wienen gjin krûden foar woeksen. Der wie noch mar ien mooglikheid: nei Dútslân, nei de wite susters yn Bremen, de wite nonnen. Dêr ha se de pasjinte—it wie in frommis—yn behanneling nommen. Se sprieken in toverformule út. Se seinen (yn 't Dútsk fansels): 'Ik beswar dy yn 'e namme fan de Heit en de Soan en de Hillige Geast, datstû fan har wykst', en al sa mear. En dan sloegen se in krús. Dat ha se in kear of wat dien en doe koe se wer nei hûs ta gean. En doe't se thuskaam, is der súntsjesoan betterskip kommen. Op 't lêst is der in stik guod út kommen as in blomkoal, sokssawat. Dat is út it boarst fallen. …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"LYST283","role":"card","render":{"description":"A minister has to walk home late in the evening through a dark wood. He has a fearful premonition that something will happen to him. And indeed, a wit wief (white woman) shows herself to him. The minister tells the figure that it may stay if it was sent by God, but must leave if it was sent by the devil. The apparition vanishes at once.","place":"Ede","prov":"Gld.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"L.C.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13627","original":"Witte Wieven\nDominee Detmar, te Ede, kwam laat terug van het bezoek bij een ouderling en moest de Witte Wieven bij Kernhem passeren. Hij voelde zich ongerust, er zou hem iets gebeuren. Toch ging hij. Op het Hooge Dennenboschje verscheen hem een witte juffer. Dominee zei: \"Ben je van God, dan staat, ben je van de duivel, dan gaat.\" En de gedaante verdween.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with N.","Nijega. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c3","object":"window","text":"Nijega"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":3,"card":"c3","word":"three","stained":"c3"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.8034,"rank":0.875,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ029903","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A bridal couple is on the way to the town hall when the bridegroom-to-be suddenly bites a piece out of his bride's apron. The man is a werewolf; the girl breaks it off at once.","place":"Kûkherne","prov":"Fr.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21918","original":"It gebeurde us dat twa jonge lju yn 'e wein sieten nei 't gemeentehûs ta. Hja soenen dy deis trouwe. Underweis yn 'e wein byt de man har in stik út 'e skelk. Hy wie in wjerwolf. Hja makke it fuort út.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ017409","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A couple about to be married take a drive in the cart. The bridegroom-to-be asks the woman whether she has a skirt for him. The woman is surprised but gives him the skirt. The man quickly makes off, but his wife follows him. She sees him tearing the skirt with his teeth; foam is around his mouth. The man confesses that he is a werewolf and had to bite into a cloth, because otherwise he would have had to attack a person. The woman calls off the wedding at once.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20171","original":"Twa jonge lju soenen trouwe. Hja makken de moarns earst in ritsje yn 'e wein.\nUnderweis sei de jonge man: \"Ik mat der even út. Hast ek in read-baeijen rôk?\"\n\"Ja, hwat matst dêr mei?\"\n\"Even brûke.\"\nHy krige de rôk, mar hja folge him stikum. Hy forskuorde de rôk en tjirge him as in wyld beest. It skûm stie him om 'e mûle. It wienen allegearre flarden read guod tusken syn tosken.\n\"Hwat hastû dien?\" frege hja.\n\"Ik sil 't dy sizze. Ik bin in wjerwolf. Nou en dan mat ik hwat forskuorre, oars forskuor ik in minske. Hja rieden togearre wer nei hûs ta.\nDoe sei hja: \"It trouwen giet oer. Ik wol net in keardel ha dy't in wjerwolf is.\"","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ044011","role":"variant","render":{"description":"One of seven sons is a werewolf. You must never quarrel with a werewolf, because then he will kill you. A girl always did sewing at other people's homes. Her suitor once asked her for a handkerchief. She gave it to him, and outside he tore the thing to shreds. After that he was normal again. He turned out to be a werewolf. Then the girl broke it off.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24049","original":"Ien fan sawn soannen wie in wjerwolf. As in wjerwolf jin kriget, makket er jin dea, seinen se froeger tsjin ús. Men mat der noait rûzje mei krije, sei in muoike yn 'e Westerein, dan pakke se jo.\nMyn wiif hat in kammeraetske hawn, dy naeide altyd by oare minsken. Dy hie forkearing mei in feint.\nOp in kear wie er by har, doe frege er har om har bûsdoek. Hja hie him de bûsdoek jown, mar doe hied er dy bûsdoek yn alle moster forskuord bûtendoar.\nLetter wie er wer goed west, mar 't is wol útrekke tusken dy beiden. Hwant hy wie in wjerwolf.\nHja hat it sels oan myn wiif forteld. Dat kammeraetske wenne oan it Wyldpaed.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Friesland an object was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1953.","That card names an object. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"0133515b4a0488e2","accepted_hashes":["98ee420cda1dfacfaaa31abf68161da38b5548538e6c72f5922a032604f6816e","de64f481c8b6da30b42d66516121b52e0a06772287f7b4e393f531b4803d57a4"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1194,"rank":0.5368,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ084112","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven girls is a nightmare and one of seven boys is a werewolf.","place":"Rottevalle","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/32830","original":"Se sizze fan 'e sawn famkes út ien húshâlding is ien in nachtmerje en fan 'e sawn jonges út in húshâlding is ien in wearwolf","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ018116","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A wit wief (white woman) haunts a certain haunted spot.","place":"Sumar","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20270","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ101519","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven daughters is a nightmare; one of seven sons is a werewolf.","place":"Drachtstercompagnie","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36981","original":"Ien fan sawn famkes út ien gesin wie in nachtmerje.\nIen fan sawn jonges út ien gesin wie in wjerwolf.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ085401","role":"member","render":{"description":"One of seven brothers is a werewolf. When he has one of his fits, you must throw him an old apron or something like it. He then tears it to pieces. If you see someone with threads hanging from his mouth, you can be sure he is a werewolf.","place":"Rottevalle","prov":"Fr.","year":1971,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33002","original":"In wearwolf is in minske, dy forropt de boel. 't Is ien fan sawn jonges (7 bruorren). As er wer sa'n kuer krijt, dat er hwat forskuorre mat, mat men him in âld skelk of sahwathinne tasmite. Us mem sei, dan gebeurde 't wol dat him even letter de triedden ta de mûle úthongen.\nAs men sa'n ien seach, dy't triedden ta de mûle út hie, koe men der fan op oan dat it in wearwolf wie. Dêr koe men se oan herkenne.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Sumar belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.0978,"rank":0.7692,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"TINNEV042","role":"card","render":{"description":"Two men are looking for grass stalks to cut. When they find none, they go home. After they have parted, one of the men suddenly sees a large wolf on his path. The next morning the other man asks him whether he saw the wolf.","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1944,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.T.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22388","original":"29.\nPeter ging op een kier met Dorus mieskes sni'je. Mao zi'j konne de gin vinne en wolle daorum weer op huus aan. De weg liep deur een buske. Dorus vroeg aan Peter offe um nao huus sol brenge. \"Loop nao da galg\", antwore Peter en kroap onder de scheibeum nève de weg hèèr.\n\"Hi'j is ter\", riep Dorus um nao. Ienéns stong d'r een grote wolf op de bosweg. Hi'j wol niet op zied gaon. Daorum drèèje Peter de met een flinken boag umhen. Toe e is umkek zag e niks meer. Umdat Peter geld neudig had ginge de 's marges weer op uut um smele te zuke. Ien Kilder was Dorus al met een groten trop aan 't sni'je. Toe hi'j Peter zag riep tem toe: \"Wasse d'r now, of niet?\".","lang":"Liemers dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LYST008","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every night at exactly twelve o'clock a farmhand takes a small hoop out of the lime tree. He hangs the hoop around his neck and turns into a werewolf. He roams about for a while and tears apart everything that comes near him. After that he becomes an ordinary person again. The farmer finds his behaviour strange and asks the priest for advice. The priest realises that the farmhand is a werewolf and advises the farmer to send the farmhand on an errand from which he can never be back home by midnight. On the agreed night the priest takes the hoop out of the tree at midnight. The farmhand is standing under that tree and sees everything. He flees and never comes back.","place":"Erp","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0803","initials":"F.W.J.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13222","original":"De Weerwolf\nEen boerenknecht kroop 's nachts klokslag 12 uur in de lindenboom voor de boerderij. Boven in de boom hing voor gewone mensen onzichtbaar een hoepeltje. Dat hing de knecht om zijn hals. Als ie uit de boom geklauterd was, liep ie in de gedaante van een hond weg en verscheurde alles wat hem in de weg kwam. Als ie een tijd zo rondgelopen had, was ie weer gewoon mens. Na een tijd was het de boer, bij wie de weerwolf in dienst was, opgevallen, dat zijn knecht nacht op nacht weg was. Hij ging naar de pastoor en die had het zaakje meteen door. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ100830","role":"door","render":{"description":"Of seven brothers, one is a werewolf. A werewolf can simply eat someone up.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"TM 3107","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36885","original":"Fan sawn bruorren út ien húshâlding is ien in wjerwolf.\nIn wjerwolf koe in oar samar opfrette.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","7 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c4","object":"door","n":7},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":2,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.648,"rank":0.477,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ015303","role":"top","render":{"description":"A man has spent an evening amusing himself with the women, and on his way home he comes upon a large, dark dog blocking his path.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0333","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19846","half":"top"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VERHOEFF001001","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"At midnight during the vigil the lamp swings, and there are footsteps and a thud. The prediction that a witch will come to watch the funeral of the dead child comes true.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"BIJLSMA007505","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"A carter sees something standing in front of his horse at a bridge; he urges his horse on, and at the bridge a figure stands before the horse. Man, horse and cart are lifted up and thrown into the canal.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KEMP324","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The girl must pray a rosary every day for a month. The girl does so, and the soul gives a sign of its release: one day as the girl is sitting in church, she suddenly sees a charred print on a handkerchief. The handkerchief is said still to be on view in the church of Meerssen.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ050510","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"When the man looks away for a moment, the animal has suddenly vanished. By daylight there are no tracks to be seen. The neighbour has also seen the animal running. It is a ghost animal.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"KEMP087","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"But whoever comes to the place at night still hears the moaning of the plague victims and sees figures wandering under the scourge of the Black Death.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"VODA_005_08","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"While doing so he finds a chest of money. The banging does not stop, however. Then he decides to ask for help from an old woman, who sprinkles the rooms with holy water. The banging goes away, and the once poor family now has the money that was left behind.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"KEMP175","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"It tells her that a treasure is hidden in the cellar: two pots of money, one of which she must give to the church and the other she may keep. From then on the woman and her husband are rich, and they sell their shop.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"LYST018","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The man asks the drunkard again and again: \"Where shall I put it?\", and the drunkard answers that he should just put the stone back where he got it. At that very moment the bearer of the boundary stone vanishes.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0404"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"CJ015303","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"Piter first waits a while to see if the dog will go away by itself. When the animal stays put, he decides simply to walk past it. Suddenly he finds himself in the ditch with the dog. A moment later the dog has vanished, and Piter runs home terrified. It was a phantom animal.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"BIJLSMA008901","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"But the beachcombers chop off both her hands to take the rings, and the woman drowns. At night skippers see the woman wandering by the post, so the murder is not forgotten.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"VODA_023_06","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"The wandering ghost of the knight lures people into the Dolle Moer. As foretold, the knight's corpse is found, in the form of, among other things, a gilded silver helmet.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"CJ101213","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"It was a plaagbeest (tormenting spectral beast), and it only went away when he took out some rye bread.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333"},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The bottom piece mentions ‘dog’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0333. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c10"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c10"],"stack":["c1","c10"]},"found_card":{"card":"c10"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1065,"rank":0.515,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"SINBRABSAG078","role":"member","render":{"description":"In Aalst, a farmer's wife's daughter saw a spirit while she was milking the cow. She was very frightened and the next day the farmhand went with her. He saw the spirit too. The spirit came closer every evening, and the priest said they should ask the spirit what it desired. The farmer's wife, the farmhand and the daughter asked the spirit what it desired, and it told them it had vowed to make a pilgrimage to Kevelaar but had never fulfilled it. They decided to make the pilgrimage all together. After the journey the spirit was released and could go to heaven.","place":"Voldijn","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1933,"code":null,"initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46713","original":"No. 78. Iederen avond ging de dochter van een boer uit Aalst met een paar meiden de koeien melken, tot zij op zekeren avond aan den rand van een bosch, op flinken afstand, een witte gedaante zag verschijnen. Ze werd bang en liep naar huis, zonder de koeien verder te melken. Ze kon niet spreken van angst en schrik, omdat ze niet wist wat 't was, en kwam hijgend van 't loopen thuis aan. De huisgenooten vroegen direct wat er aan de hand was, en toen zei ze, na tot bedaren gekomen te zijn, dat 't kon gaan zooals 't wilde, maar ze ging niet meer alleen melken, zoo was ze geschrokken. Den volgenden avond ging de knecht mee, omdat ze alleen niet meer wilde. Ze zagen dezelfde gedaante weer, maar nu kwam ze veel dichter bij. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"SINBRABSAG080","role":"member","render":{"description":"A poor broom-maker saw the spirit of his father, who had recently died, sitting on the wheelbarrow. His father told him he had to make a pilgrimage and give bread to the poor, because his father had made a vow that he had not kept. After these words his father disappeared.","place":"Eersel","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1933,"code":null,"initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46715","original":"No. 80. Omstreeks 1840 ging de arme bezembinder R. v. G. uit Eersel hei snijden. Nadat hij zijn vracht op de kruiwagen geladen had, rustte hij in de Zanddreef wat uit. Toen hij zijn tocht wilde voortzetten zat de geest van zijn vader, die voor kort gestorven was, op z'n kruiwagen. Hij beval zijn zoon om een beevaart te doen en den armen een brood te geven, want hij had tijdens zijn leven, een belofte niet nagekomen. Daarop verdween de geest, zonder een spoor achter te laten. 2)","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"SINBRABSAG081","role":"member","render":{"description":"The spirit of the priest asks a pious person whether she will do a good work for him, so that he can enter heaven.","place":"Westerhoven","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1933,"code":null,"initials":"I.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/46716","original":"No. 81. Het gebeurde op het gehucht Loveren, anderen zeggen in het braambosch, onder Westerhoven. De pastoor was gestorven, en zijn geest verscheen aan een vroom kwezelken, en verzocht haar spoedig een goed werk voor hem te laten doen, dan zou hij zalig worden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ039817","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A man asks his sweetheart for a handkerchief and disappears with it. When he returns, red threads from the handkerchief hang between his teeth. He confesses that he is a werewolf who must tear something apart now and then, and had asked for a handkerchief so as not to tear her apart.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/23534","original":"Der wienen in feint en in faem, dy wienen togearre út to riden.\nUnderweis lei de feint de swipe del en hy liet it hynder stilstean.\nDe faem sei tsjin 'e feint: \"Hwat silstû?\"\n\"Jow my de bûsdoek\", sei er. Doe joech se him in reade bûsdoek. Dêr gong er mei fuort.\nDoe't er in skoftsje fuort west hie, kom er werom. Doe hied er de reade triedden fan 'e bûsdoek tusken de tosken hingjen.\n\"Hwat hastû dien?\" sei se.\nDoe hied er bikend dat er in wjerwolf wie. Hy moest nou en dan hwat forskuorre. Dêrom hied er om 'e bûsdoek frege, oars hied er har forskuorre matten.\nDoe hat dy faem de forkearing gau út makke.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:3"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a werewolf.","The card about Harkema belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c4","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.1385,"rank":0.5,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ096704","role":"top","render":{"description":"One evening the narrator's man and his cousin had been to the inn 'De laatste Stuver'.","place":"Buitenpost","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0333","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36136","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"BOEKV147","role":"half","render":{"description":"The ghosts pull up a kettle of gold coins and hide it again. In the morning the soldier asks the farmhand to help him dig. By the haystack they find the kettle of gold and take it. At night the ghosts come to dig again, but find nothing and never return. The farmer is pleased and offers the soldier lodging and a reward. The soldier accepts the lodging, but by now he has enough money.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0401"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ101206","role":"half","render":{"description":"She asked whether the beast came from the Lord or from Satan. If it came from the devil, it had to clear off. The beast disappeared.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ096704","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"When they were standing on a bridge, they saw an animal coming across the meadow. The animal was pitch black and as big as a cow. It had the shape of a dog. The beast looked at the two men. They became so frightened that they quickly ran off.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333","stain":"two"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"DYKFRIES2153","role":"half","render":{"description":"When she was warned about the ghost foal, she claimed she would put her garter in its mouth and ride it home. But when she actually met the animal, she was terrified and ran home.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0333"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ046110","role":"half","render":{"description":"The shopkeeper does not believe it, but shortly afterwards he is startled by the ghost of the dead husband.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0450"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1256","role":"half","render":{"description":"One of those farmers could do witchcraft, and he was in the Oude Straat at night with horse and cart when suddenly two cats jumped out in front.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘man’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0333. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c4","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c4"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":2,"card":"c1","word":"two","stained":"c4"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
